---
title: Chart of accounts
description: Your accounts, ready from day one, and the system accounts nullish books on for you.
---

When you create an organization, nullish sets up a complete chart of accounts for its legal form: one for LLCs and corporations, one for sole proprietorships. You'll find it under **Settings → Accounting → Accounts**.

## Accounts

Each account has a **Code**, a **Name** and a **Type**: **Assets**, **Liabilities**, **Equity**, **Income**, **Expenses** or **Closing**. Accounts can be grouped under a **Parent account**, e.g. `1020 Bank` sits in the group of liquid assets.

- You book on the accounts at the bottom of the tree. Groups only add up what's below them.
- Leave the **Name** empty to keep the standard name, translated into your language.
- Need an account that isn't there? Choose **Create account**.

{% aside %}
To keep your books consistent, an account can't be deleted once it has postings or sub-accounts,
or is used as a system account. Its type can't change once it has postings either.
{% /aside %}

## System accounts

Some bookings happen automatically: opening an invoice, recording a payment, writing off a debt, closing the year. nullish needs to know which account to use for each of them. That's what **System accounts** are for, under **Settings → Accounting → System accounts**.

They come preset, so you usually don't need to touch them. The ones nullish books on today:

| System account          | Default                                 | Used when                                            |
| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| Debtors                 | 1100                                    | an invoice is opened, paid or written off            |
| Default income          | 3400                                    | an invoice is opened                                 |
| VAT due                 | 2200                                    | an invoice or entry carries VAT                      |
| Bank account            | 1020                                    | a payment is recorded without picking a bank account |
| Creditors               | 2300                                    | a client pays too much                               |
| Bad debts               | 3805                                    | an invoice is written off                            |
| Rounding differences    | 6945                                    | amounts need rounding to the cent                    |
| Exchange gains / losses | 6999 / 6949                             | a foreign-currency payment differs from the invoice  |
| Annual profit or loss   | 9200                                    | the year is closed                                   |
| Annual result (equity)  | 2979, or 2891 for a sole proprietorship | the year is closed                                   |

To use another account, for example a separate income account, choose **Edit** and pick it.
